// ed047tc1/ sibling directory.
//
// This is epdiy's MODE_DU (type=1) table for the ED047TC1 panel, byte-for-byte
// from vroland/epdiy's src/waveforms/epdiy_ED047TC1.h. 5 phases; each phase's
// LUT is 16 "to" nibble values x 4 bytes packing all 16 "from" nibble values
// at 2 bits/entry -- a genuine (from,to) transition table, not the
// target-only scheme ed047tc1/epd_driver.c uses. All 5 phases carry identical
// LUT content in the source data: MODE_DU pushes a fixed direction/duration
// per (from,to) pair regardless of frame index, which is why it converges in
// far fewer phases than a target-only waveform and tolerates an arbitrary
// starting value. Only black (to=0) and white (to=15) rows are populated --
// MODE_DU is B/W-target only, matching this driver's B/W-only content.
//
// Consumed by Ed047Tc1DiffWaveform.{h,cpp}, not by anything in vendor/ed047tc1/.

